Licensing note for the webrarian package
========================================

webrarian is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
(AGPL-3), as the License field of DESCRIPTION says. That covers the R code in
R/, the tests, the documentation, the templates in inst/templates/ and the
example projects in inst/examples/. R ships the license text
(share/licenses/AGPL-3); it is also at https://www.R-project.org/Licenses/AGPL-3.

Additional permission under GNU AGPL version 3 section 7 (output exception)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The files that webrarian writes into a generated site or mirror — including
content derived from its templates — are not covered by the GNU AGPL merely
because webrarian produced them. You may license and distribute that output
under terms of your choice. Third-party components copied into the output (the
exlibris runtime, the webR/Pyodide engine, and R or Python packages) remain
under their own licenses, which the output's `LICENSES/` directory records.

This permission is in addition to the AGPL. Under section 7 of the AGPL anyone
who conveys webrarian may remove it from their copy, so the License field states
the AGPL alone: those rights hold whether or not the permission is kept.

The same permission is installed with the package as OUTPUT-EXCEPTION.md
(inst/OUTPUT-EXCEPTION.md in the sources), and bind() and collection_mirror()
write it into every site's and mirror's LICENSES/webrarian.md.

Vendored browser bundle in inst/viewer/
---------------------------------------

inst/viewer/exlibris-r.js and inst/viewer/exlibris-r.css are the prebuilt,
minified build output of the exlibris runtime
(https://github.com/coatless-wasm/exlibris) at v0.1.3, commit
04767100e2f642f14ddd5e5a84064e7edef3cc6d (exlibris 0.1.3). Their source is that commit:
https://github.com/coatless-wasm/exlibris/tree/04767100e2f642f14ddd5e5a84064e7edef3cc6d
exlibris is licensed AGPL-3.0-only with the exlibris runtime exception
(inst/viewer/EXCEPTION.md), which lets generated sites carry the unmodified
bundles under terms of their author's choice.

    exlibris-r.js   sha256 3b8bf5477cf56f158c97ffb04ad576abbfcdc1b99ff6198224ebf042bf870cfc
    exlibris-r.css  sha256 22ae9ccc0062abd0f9682547c54fbbaa4798c3beb836f0454f56945eea5f2b70

inst/viewer/PROVENANCE.json records the same commit and digests.
tools/vendor-exlibris.sh writes this file, inst/viewer/THIRD-PARTY.md and
inst/viewer/LICENSE.webR.md from it on every re-vendor.

Embedded third-party components
-------------------------------

The bundle embeds code from npm packages under permissive licenses (MIT, ISC,
BSD-3-Clause, zlib and Apache-2.0) and CC BY 4.0 icon path data. Their copyright
holders are credited with the "cph" role in the Authors@R field of DESCRIPTION
and listed in inst/COPYRIGHTS. inst/viewer/THIRD-PARTY.md lists every package
with its version and license and reproduces each license text.
inst/viewer/LICENSE.webR.md covers the webR JavaScript client (webR
0.6.0, MIT).
